# Hippiatrica Berolinensia - English translation, batch 26
# global indices 1625-1689 (65 items)
# Section: closing anecdote of the Book Two proem (Aristotle on a horse that
# killed itself after unknowingly mating with its own mother) -> "On an
# ulcerated mouth" -> "On aphtha/mouth-thrush" (Hierocles; two variants, with
# and without ulceration) -> "On exhaustion from a journey or run and on
# drawing pain in the flanks" (Apsyrtus to Marcus Aemilius) -> "Prognosis and
# cure of kopos (exhaustion)" (a long passage on distinguishing exhaustion
# from fever, colic and opisthotonos by their signs; Celsus, Florus) -> "On
